  "addlInstrHelpText": "These sections are all optional. Use them to give guidance to your agent and treatment team beyond the basic preferences above.",
  "addlInstrExampleFieldName": "Additional Instructions",
  "addlInstrExample1": "I find listening to calming music and going for walks helpful during periods of distress. Please allow me access to my personal music player.",
  "addlInstrExample2": "I am vegetarian for religious reasons. Please ensure my dietary needs are respected during any inpatient stay. I would also like access to a chaplain or spiritual advisor.",
  "addlInstrExample3": "Please notify my sister, Jane Doe, if I am admitted. Do not contact my ex-spouse under any circumstances. My therapist, Dr. Smith, should be informed of any treatment changes.",
  "addlInstrActivitiesTitle": "Activities & Environment",
  "addlInstrActivitiesHint": "Preferences about daily activities, environment, restraints, seclusion",
  "addlInstrActivitiesDescription": "Describe activities that help you feel better (e.g., walking, reading, music) and your preferences about your physical environment during treatment. You can also state whether you consent to or refuse the use of restraints (being physically held or strapped down, or given medication to restrict your movement or behavior — a \"chemical restraint\") or seclusion (being confined alone in a room).",
  "addlInstrCrisisTitle": "Crisis Intervention",
  "addlInstrCrisisHint": "What helps or doesn't help during a crisis",
  "addlInstrCrisisDescription": "Based on your past experience, describe what helps you during a mental health crisis and what makes things worse. This helps your treatment team respond in the way that works best for you.",
  "addlInstrDeescTitle": "De-escalation Techniques",
  "addlInstrDeescHint": "e.g., music, deep breathing, quiet room, weighted blanket",
  "addlInstrDeescDescription": "List specific techniques or strategies that help calm you when you are distressed. Examples include listening to music, deep breathing, being in a quiet room, using a weighted blanket, speaking with a specific person, or going for a walk.",
  "addlInstrTriggersTitle": "Potential Crisis Triggers",
  "addlInstrTriggersHint": "e.g., loud environments, specific topics, being alone",
  "addlInstrTriggersDescription": "Identify situations, environments, or topics that may trigger or worsen a crisis for you. This helps your treatment team avoid these triggers. Examples: loud environments, being touched without permission, certain conversation topics, being left alone, or specific people.",
  "addlInstrHealthHistoryTitle": "Health History",
  "addlInstrHealthHistoryHint": "Relevant mental health history, diagnoses, hospitalizations",
  "addlInstrHealthHistoryDescription": "Summarize your relevant mental health history, including past diagnoses, hospitalizations, and treatments that worked well or did not work. This gives your treatment team context about your care history.",
  "addlInstrDietaryTitle": "Dietary Preferences",
  "addlInstrDietaryHint": "Food restrictions, preferences, religious dietary laws",
  "addlInstrDietaryDescription": "List any food allergies, dietary restrictions, or preferences your treatment team should know about. This includes religious dietary laws (e.g., kosher, halal, vegetarian), food intolerances, and any foods to avoid due to medication interactions.",
  "addlInstrReligiousTitle": "Religious & Spiritual",
  "addlInstrReligiousHint": "Religious practices, spiritual needs, clergy contact",
  "addlInstrReligiousDescription": "Describe any religious or spiritual practices that are important to you during treatment. This may include prayer times, clergy or chaplain visits, religious texts or items you would like to have access to, fasting observances, or faith-based coping practices.",
  "addlInstrChildrenTitle": "Children & Custody",
  "addlInstrChildrenHint": "Instructions regarding care of your minor children",
  "addlInstrChildrenDescription": "If you have minor children or dependents, describe who should care for them if you are hospitalized. Include contact information for caregivers, school details, and any custody arrangements your treatment team should be aware of.",
  "addlInstrFamilyNotifyTitle": "Family Notification",
  "addlInstrFamilyNotifyHint": "Who should be notified and how",
  "addlInstrFamilyNotifyDescription": "Specify who should be notified if you are hospitalized or if your treatment changes. Include how to reach them and what information may be shared. You can also specify people who should NOT be contacted.",
  "addlInstrPetCareTitle": "Pet Care",
  "addlInstrPetCareHint": "Instructions for care of your pets",
  "addlInstrPetCareDescription": "If you have pets, describe who should care for them if you are hospitalized. Include the caregiver's contact information, feeding and medication schedules, veterinary contacts, and any special care instructions.",
  "addlInstrReproTitle": "Reproductive Health Care",
  "addlInstrReproHint": "Pregnancy testing, contraception, etc.",
  "addlInstrReproDescription": "Describe any reproductive health care preferences your treatment team should know about. This may include whether you want pregnancy testing before medication changes, contraception preferences, or reproductive health conditions that could affect your treatment.",
  "addlInstrOtherTitle": "Other Instructions",
  "addlInstrOtherHint": "Any other instructions not covered above",
  "addlInstrOtherDescription": "Use this section for any instructions to your treatment team or agent that are not covered by the sections above. This is a catch-all for anything else you want to communicate about your care preferences.",
  "addlInstrRecordsTitle": "Records Disclosure & Limitations",
  "addlInstrRecordsDescription": "Choose who may — and may not — receive copies of your mental health records. Under 20 Pa.C.S. § 5836(e), the disclosure authority you grant here can override certain confidentiality protections (including drug & alcohol, mental-health-procedures, and HIV confidentiality laws), so be specific.",
  "addlInstrRecordsReleaseLabel": "Who may receive my records",
  "addlInstrRecordsReleaseHint": "e.g. my agent Jane Doe; my treatment team; Dr. Smith",
  "addlInstrRecordsWithholdLabel": "Who must NOT receive my records",
  "addlInstrRecordsWithholdHint": "e.g. my ex-spouse; specific family members",
  "addlInstrRecordsOtherLabel": "Other limitations on disclosure",
  "addlInstrRecordsOtherHint": "e.g. release only records from the last 12 months",
  "addlInstrOptionalAddOns": "Optional add-ons",
  "addlInstrCrisisPlanTitle": "Crisis plan",
  "addlInstrCrisisPlanSubtitle": "Your early-warning signs, triggers, what genuinely helps, and what not to do. Not required by Act 194 — but it's the part agents and ER staff read first.",
  "addlInstrUlyssesTitle": "Self-binding (Ulysses) clause",
  "addlInstrUlyssesSubtitle": "Acknowledge that, once two professionals find you incapable, what you wrote stands even over your in-the-moment protest, until capacity returns (20 Pa.C.S. §§ 5824, 5834).",
  "effCondHelpText": "Describe the circumstances under which you want this directive to take effect — for example, \"when two qualified professionals certify that I lack capacity to make treatment decisions.\" Under PA Act 194, the declaration becomes operative when a psychiatrist and one of the following certify you lack capacity: another psychiatrist, a licensed psychologist, your family physician, your attending physician, or another mental health treatment professional.",
  "effCondTakeEffectWhen": "This directive should take effect when…",
  "effCondTriggerTwoTitle": "A psychiatrist + one other professional find I lack capacity",
  "effCondTriggerTwoSubtitle": "The standard PA Act 194 trigger — two qualified professionals certify you can't make mental-health treatment decisions.",
  "effCondTriggerCourtTitle": "A court determines I lack capacity",
  "effCondTriggerCommitTitle": "I am involuntarily committed",
  "effCondAnythingElseTitle": "Anything else about timing (optional)",
  "effCondAnythingElseSubtitle": "Add your own words, or pick an example to start from.",
  "effCondExampleFieldName": "Effective Condition",
  "effCondExample1": "This directive takes effect when I am unable to make mental health treatment decisions for myself, as determined by two qualified professionals.",
  "effCondExample2": "This directive becomes effective any time I am admitted to a psychiatric facility or crisis unit, whether voluntary or involuntary, and I am unable to clearly communicate my wishes.",
  "effCondExample3": "This directive takes effect when I am experiencing a severe episode of psychosis, mania, or dissociation that prevents me from understanding my treatment options or communicating my preferences.",
  "effCondExample4": "This directive becomes effective when I tell my agent or treatment provider that I want it activated, or when I am unable to make consistent and informed decisions about my mental health care.",
  "effCondExample5": "This directive is effective when my designated agent, in consultation with any treating professional, determines that I would benefit from having my pre-stated treatment preferences followed.",
